================================================================================
Academic Research & Methodological Credits
================================================================================

Cohezion operationalizes algorithms, theorems, and methodologies from the
following published scientific works:

- AutoHarness: "Deterministic Code-as-Action Verifiers and Bytecode Policy Synthesis"
  (arXiv:2603.03329v1).
- LLM-to-Flow Distillation (LFD): "Teaching Natural Language Goals to Scientific Generators"
  by De Santi, Di Gennaro, Gnazzo, Tang, Chatterjee, Yang, Ceylan, Bronstein, Krause (arXiv:2610.17246, 2026).
- Terminal-RSI: "Success-Prioritized Reward (SPR) in Recursive Self-Improvement" (arXiv:2610.22192, 2026).
- Weight-Harness Co-Evolution (Evo^2 / EvoTIDE): "Dual-Role Policy Decomposition" (arXiv:2610.12842, 2026).
- Stafford Beer: The Viable System Model (VSM) from "Brain of the Firm" (1972) and
  "The Heart of Enterprise" (1979).
- W. Ross Ashby: The Law of Requisite Variety from "An Introduction to Cybernetics" (1956).
- R.C. Conant & W.R. Ashby: "Every good regulator of a system must be a model of that system"
  (International Journal of Systems Science, 1970).
- Henri Poincaré: Hyperbolic Disc and Manifold Geometry (1882).
- Roger Penrose & Stuart Hameroff: Orchestrated Objective Reduction (Orch-OR) & Twistor Theory (1996).
- Ilya Prigogine: Dissipative Structures and Non-Equilibrium Thermodynamics (1977).
- Claude E. Shannon: "A Mathematical Theory of Communication" (1948).
- John von Neumann: Theory of Self-Reproducing Automata (1966).
- Leslie Lamport: Logical Clocks, Paxos, and Distributed Systems Consensus (1978).
- Barbara McClintock: Transposable Genetic Elements and Dynamic Regulation (1950).

For full bibliography and dataset terms of use, see ATTRIBUTION.md.
